{title: Eternal Father, Strong to Save}
{artist: William Whiting & John Dykes}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 76}

Verse 1
E[C]ternal Father, [Am]strong to [G]save, whose [Am]arm hath bound the [D]restless [G]wave,
who [C]bidd'st the mighty [F]ocean [C]deep its [D]own appointed [G]limits keep:
O [C]hear us when we [F]cry to [C]thee for [F]those in [C]peril [G]on the [C]sea.
